# WN22-DC-000410: Windows Server 2022 Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000410-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services user right on domain controllers must be configured to prevent unauthenticated access.`
    description `Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities. The "Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services" user right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on using Remote Desktop Services. The Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,user-rights,security-policy,ksi-iam-elp,ksi-mla-let,ksi-mla-osm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-MLA-OSM,NIST-800-53:AC-17(1)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-ELP,KSI-MLA-LET,KSI-MLA-OSM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services to include the following: - Guests Group`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_ELP `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-ELP by requiring the SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight user right to include at least the SIDs [S-1-5-32-546] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-LET by requiring the SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight user right to include at least the SIDs [S-1-5-32-546] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-OSM by requiring the SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight user right to include at least the SIDs [S-1-5-32-546] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_17_1 `Windows Server implements AC-17(1) by requiring the SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight user right to include at least the SIDs [S-1-5-32-546] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `SeDenyRemoteInteractiveLogonRight`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE has_sid_1
        exists boolean = true
        value string contains `*S-1-5-32-546`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF has_sid_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
